{"title":"2006 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 21","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Rectangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> has area <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/2/d1216dd3855e1bb88b6136b4ce49c58b57747417.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2006$\" width=\"35\" height=\"12\" />.  An ellipse with area <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/d/12d0f141a4950a55a46eed31ee659daf8cf909d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2006\\pi$\" width=\"46\" height=\"12\" /> passes through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and has foci at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />.  What is the perimeter of the rectangle? (The area of an ellipse is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/0/6801049254e97b2fe75bfc4410f1184945956dec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ab\\pi$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/6/6c6ea4756efa52a156029529aba37a305a5cb496.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/b/a9b30259d95f64f9aa7c6bd36e1583618a23c8bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"14\" /> are the lengths of the axes.)\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/5/955c5e4f2621cea32b853cde718f8b0c1ceec38b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A)}\\ \\frac {16\\sqrt {2006}}{\\pi} \\qquad \\mathrm{(B)}\\ \\frac {1003}4 \\qquad \\mathrm{(C)}\\ 8\\sqrt {1003} \\qquad \\mathrm{(D)}\\ 6\\sqrt {2006} \\qquad \\mathrm{(E)}\\ \\frac {32\\sqrt {1003}}\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"604\" height=\"41\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/5/905e36368530c426cb71e1619e8af231adb4aa63.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(7cm);  real l=10, w=7, ang=asin(w/sqrt(l*l+w*w))*180/pi;  draw((-l,-w)--(l,-w)--(l,w)--(-l,w)--cycle); draw(rotate(ang)*ellipse((0,0),2*l+2*w,l*w*2/sqrt(l^2+w^2)));  draw(rotate(ang)*((0,0)--(2l+2w,0)),red); draw(rotate(ang+90)*((0,0)--(l*w*2/sqrt(l^2+w^2),0)),red);  label(&quot;$A$&quot;,(-l,w),NW); label(&quot;$B$&quot;,(-l,-w),SW); label(&quot;$C$&quot;,(l,-w),SE); label(&quot;$D$&quot;,(l,w),SE); // Made by chezbgone2 [/asy]\" width=\"332\" height=\"252\" />\n</p><p>Let the rectangle have side lengths <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/2/9b25f8e64b484493fda944d25cad453423041fe6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l$\" width=\"5\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/e/9ee4b825a2e36ae093ed7be5e4851ef453b34914.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" />.  Let the axis of the ellipse on which the foci lie have length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/6/6c6ea4756efa52a156029529aba37a305a5cb496.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" />, and let the other axis have length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/b/a9b30259d95f64f9aa7c6bd36e1583618a23c8bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"14\" />.  We have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/c/64ca5cb3ac715ad0642585f852b24b5a23c6ba4f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[lw=ab=2006\\]\" width=\"120\" height=\"12\" />\nFrom the definition of an ellipse, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/d/57d53aba4f416592458489e17d4b197f52740fe2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l+w=2a\\Longrightarrow \\frac{l+w}{2}=a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"203\" height=\"37\" />.  Also, the diagonal of the rectangle has length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/b/e1bedadf1cd5b9bcf61cff42b419af42bf8d1013.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{l^2+w^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"71\" height=\"18\" />.  Comparing the lengths of the axes and the distance from the foci to the center, we have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/d/55db6690aa38e6203cda73957eec187e9696b385.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a^2=\\frac{l^2+w^2}{4}+b^2\\Longrightarrow \\frac{l^2+2lw+w^2}{4}=\\frac{l^2+w^2}{4}+b^2\\Longrightarrow \\frac{lw}{2}=b^2\\Longrightarrow b=\\sqrt{1003}\\]\" width=\"620\" height=\"39\" />\nSince <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/9/db991caab869bfd9d2165e1e111372f3949475e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ab=2006$\" width=\"77\" height=\"12\" />, we now know <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/c/facc0957ababc8aa66fcb117136bf5dc7760ebae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\sqrt{1003}=2006\\Longrightarrow a=2\\sqrt{1003}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"255\" height=\"18\" /> and because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/c/56ca08e76b650cf19d057268b9940b1814b41681.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=\\frac{l+w}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"78\" height=\"37\" />, or one-fourth of the rectangle's perimeter, we multiply by four to get an answer of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/f/20f78360c5a006a24301e55fd2ccd41a2250b5cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{8\\sqrt{1003}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"72\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12B\" title=\"2006 AMC 12B\">2006 AMC 12B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12B_Problems\" title=\"2006 AMC 12B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2006 AMC 12B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2006 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 20\">Problem 20</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2006 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 22\">Problem 22</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2006 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2006 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2006 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2006 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2006 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2006 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2006 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2006 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2006 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2006 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2006 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2006 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2006 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2006 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2006 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</